{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018KjGuSV8eV2A7yKoWsKtu4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Let me analyze this research project carefully to define three tiers for the Dream simulation.\n\nThe project is a diagnostic analysis paper for CoRL 2026 (deadline 2026-05-29) investigating why temporal abstraction fails in DreamerV3's world-model RL. The core mechanism identified is \"Conditioning-Induced Value Overestimation\" (CIVO) triggered by trained dt_embedding.\n\nKey current state:\n1. Walker Walk experiments are largely done - strong evidence for CIVO mechanism\n2. Full-SGS (exp_018) confirmed CIVO is gradient-level phenomenon (NVE 1.00×)\n\n\n3. Cross-environment validation is underway with Cheetah Run and ManiSkill3/PickCube, while I've refined the claims from \"necessary and sufficient\" to \"necessary condition\" based on emerging evidence that C6 (dt=1 imagination) only partially mitigates the issue due to multiple vulnerability pathways.\n\nSeveral experiments are in progress or queued - Cheetah Run, the ManiSkill3 variants, and a vanilla DreamerV3 baseline - with pathway B control experiments still needing design work.\n\nNow I'm planning a threshold sensitivity analysis for the vulnerability effect metric that requires no GPU resources, and thinking through what the remaining experiments need to demonstrate: whether CIVO generalizes across environments, whether the full-SGS mechanism holds up across different seeds and settings, how to characterize the non-CIVO collapse pathway, and whether the 1.5x NVE threshold remains discriminative in new environments.\n\nI'm laying out three outcome scenarios based on what these experiments might show. The best case would confirm CIVO as a general architectural vulnerability with proven gradient-level mechanisms across both new environments and additional seeds. The median case assumes Cheetah replicates cleanly but ManiSkill3 shows ambiguous results due to different dynamics that might elevate NVE without clear separation.\n\nThe worst case is if Cheetah itself doesn't replicate with a clean CIVO signature, Full-SGS behaves unexpectedly in new seeds, and the multiple pathways story collapses into just noise—forcing me to reframe this as a single-environment mechanistic study rather than something generalizable.\n\nNow I'm defining the specific NVE thresholds I need to track across environments to validate these scenarios.\n\nWriting YAML config...","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41078,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41078},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ac7ec2d-7300-4ab7-8d3f-c38f79bfc96e","uuid":"7942a8ba-c8b7-4782-a89b-0c156b589874"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_018KjGuSV8eV2A7yKoWsKtu4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"```yaml\ntiers:\n  best:\n    meaning: \"Cross-environment CIVO replication + gradient-level mechanism fully closed\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Cheetah Run (010b) replicates NVE>1.5x with trained dt_emb at 35K+ steps\"\n      - \"ManiSkill3 PickCube (019b) shows CIVO signature despite different observation/action space\"\n      - \"Full-SGS (018) NVE≤1.0 replicates in Cheetah/PickCube (gradient-level mechanism generalizes)\"\n      - \"NVE 1.5x threshold maintains ≥3/4 separating power in each new environment\"\n      - \"Pathway B (008e_v3_s2-type eval-driven collapse) is either rare (≤1/4 cross-env) or gets clean mechanistic characterization via control experiment\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cheetah_civo_nve_35K_plus: [1.6, 3.5]\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_nve_35K_plus: [0.3, 0.9]\n      cheetah_full_sgs_nve_peak: [0.4, 1.0]\n      pickcube_civo_nve_35K_plus: [1.5, 4.0]\n      cross_env_threshold_accuracy: [0.83, 1.0]  # ≥5/6 correct classification\n      cross_env_civo_collapse_rate: [0.33, 0.67]  # consistent with Walker's 1/2\n      full_sgs_nve_cross_env_max: [0.5, 1.0]\n      environments_with_confirmed_civo: [3, 3]\n    narrative_direction: \"CIVO is a general architectural vulnerability in imagination-based actor-critic with dt-conditioning. Gradient decomposition + Full-SGS intervention proves the causal chain at mechanism level (observation decoder→dt_emb gradient drives CIVO). Cross-3-environment replication elevates from 'DreamerV3-specific finding' to 'structural warning for the temporal-abstraction-in-world-models research agenda'. TAWM contrast (MPC succeeds, imagination fails) is the headline novelty. Claims: trained dt_embedding is a necessary causal factor for CIVO; Full-SGS eliminates it; the vulnerability generalizes across DMC locomotion and manipulation.\"\n\n  median:\n    meaning: \"Cheetah replicates cleanly but ManiSkill3 is ambiguous; mechanism evidence strong in Walker only\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Cheetah Run replicates CIVO (NVE>1.5x with trained dt_emb)\"\n      - \"ManiSkill3 shows degradation but NVE stays in gray zone (1.2-1.5x) or collapse doesn't occur within budget\"\n      - \"Full-SGS holds in Walker (already confirmed) but untested or borderline in other envs due to GPU/time constraints\"\n      - \"NVE 1.5x threshold works in Cheetah but needs environment-specific calibration for manipulation tasks\"\n      - \"Pathway B remains under-characterized — acknowledged as open question, not fully resolved\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cheetah_civo_nve_35K_plus: [1.5, 2.5]\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_nve_35K_plus: [0.4, 1.1]\n      cheetah_full_sgs_nve_peak: [0.5, 1.2]  # maybe slightly above 1.0\n      pickcube_civo_nve_35K_plus: [1.0, 1.6]  # ambiguous zone\n      cross_env_threshold_accuracy: [0.67, 0.83]  # 4/6, threshold needs tuning\n      cross_env_civo_collapse_rate: [0.25, 0.50]  # maybe lower in manipulation\n      full_sgs_nve_cross_env_max: [0.7, 1.3]\n      environments_with_confirmed_civo: [2, 2]  # Walker + Cheetah only\n    narrative_direction: \"CIVO mechanism confirmed in DMC locomotion (Walker + Cheetah) with gradient-level causal evidence. ManiSkill3 results are 'consistent with but do not independently confirm' the mechanism — different observation modality (visual/proprioceptive) may modulate CIVO severity. Adjust claims: scope primary findings to RSSM + proprioceptive DMC; discuss ManiSkill3 as preliminary extension. Weaken 'generalizes across architectures' to 'generalizes within DMC locomotion; further investigation needed for manipulation/visual domains'. Pathway B acknowledged as 'trained dt_embedding creates multiple vulnerability pathways — CIVO is the dominant but not sole mechanism'. Add paragraph discussing when the 1.5x threshold may need recalibration. Paper still publishable at CoRL as strong 2-environment mechanistic diagnosis + practical warning.\"\n\n  worst:\n    meaning: \"Cheetah doesn't cleanly replicate CIVO pattern; stuck with single-environment evidence\"\n    key_assumptions:\n      - \"Cheetah Run shows performance degradation with dt>1 but NVE pattern differs (e.g., value suppression like dt=4 Walker, or gradual decline without acceleration)\"\n      - \"ManiSkill3 either fails to train or shows no clear CIVO signature\"\n      - \"NVE 1.5x threshold doesn't separate trained/untrained in Cheetah (false negatives or different dynamics)\"\n      - \"Full-SGS in Cheetah shows NVE>1.0 or unexpected interaction with different reward structure\"\n      - \"Pathway B control experiment reveals 008e_v3_s2 collapse was closer to random seed variance than a systematic second pathway\"\n    number_ranges:\n      cheetah_civo_nve_35K_plus: [0.8, 1.4]  # degradation without clear CIVO\n      cheetah_no_dt_emb_nve_35K_plus: [0.6, 1.2]  # poor separation\n      cheetah_full_sgs_nve_peak: [0.9, 1.5]  # mechanism may not transfer\n      pickcube_civo_nve_35K_plus: [0.5, 1.2]  # no signal\n      cross_env_threshold_accuracy: [0.50, 0.67]  # near chance for new envs\n      cross_env_civo_collapse_rate: [0.0, 0.33]  # maybe no collapse in Cheetah\n      full_sgs_nve_cross_env_max: [1.0, 1.8]\n      environments_with_confirmed_civo: [1, 1]  # Walker only\n    narrative_direction: \"Reframe from 'general architectural vulnerability' to 'deep mechanistic case study in Walker Walk revealing environment-specific interaction between RSSM fidelity and dt-conditioning'. The contribution becomes: (1) first rigorous factorial diagnosis of WHY temporal abstraction fails in a specific world-model RL setup, (2) introduction of NVE diagnostic methodology (validated in Walker, proposed for broader use), (3) gradient-level causal evidence (Full-SGS) that the failure is not reward-driven but observation-decoder-driven — a non-obvious finding even if environment-specific. Lean into TAWM contrast harder: 'dt-conditioning succeeds in MPC (TAWM) but fails in imagination — we provide the first mechanistic explanation for this discrepancy, demonstrated in Walker Walk with controlled factorial design'. Drop cross-environment generalization claims entirely. Add 'limitations and future work' section discussing why Cheetah dynamics differ (reward density, state dimensionality, RSSM fidelity characteristics) — turn the negative into diagnostic insight. Still viable for CoRL as methodology + single-environment depth paper, but weaker acceptance odds; may need exceptional writing quality and the TAWM contrast to carry novelty.\"\n```"}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":41078,"cache_read_input_tokens":11447,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":41078},"output_tokens":9,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"0ac7ec2d-7300-4ab7-8d3f-c38f79bfc96e","uuid":"64a5592d-7d9c-4671-bd6f-f7f38817b50f"}
